<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>West Virginia Defeats South Carolina to Win Sun Belt Tournament Title</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/mens-soccer-west-virginia-defeats-south-carolina-to-win-sun-belt-tournament-title</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/mens-soccer-west-virginia-defeats-south-carolina-to-win-sun-belt-tournament-title</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Sun Belt Tournament Champions" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/15/MSOC_vsUSC_Nov15_2026_AM-104.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 7 West Virginia University men's soccer team claimed its second trophy of the season on Sunday with a 4-0 win over South Carolina in the Sun Belt Tournament Final. The Mountaineers improve to 13-2-4 overall this season while the Gamecocks fall to 12-6-2. It is the second time in three seasons that West Virginia has swept the Sun Belt titles and is also the seventh conference tournament championship in program history.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/15/MSOC_vsUSC_Nov15_2026_AM-104.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/15/MSOC_vsUSC_Nov15_2026_AM-104.jpg"><media:title>Sun Belt Tournament Champions</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/15/MSOC_vsUSC_Nov15_2026_AM-104.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:03:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59707</s:story_id></item><item><title>No. 23 West Virginia Defeats Brown, Hofstra to Remain Undefeated</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/wrestling-no-23-west-virginia-defeats-brown-hofstra-to-remain-undefeated</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/wrestling-no-23-west-virginia-defeats-brown-hofstra-to-remain-undefeated</guid><category>Wrestling</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The No. 23 West Virginia University wrestling team dominated Mercyhurst, 52-0, to open dual competition at Cameron High School in Cameron, W.Va., on Saturday." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/7/Wrestling_vsMercyhurst_atCameron_Nov7_2026_AM-50.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 23 West Virginia University wrestling team swept a tri-meet against Brown and Hofstra at the Pizzitola Sports Center in Providence, Rhode Island, on Sunday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/7/Wrestling_vsMercyhurst_atCameron_Nov7_2026_AM-50.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/7/Wrestling_vsMercyhurst_atCameron_Nov7_2026_AM-50.jpg"><media:title>The No. 23 West Virginia University wrestling team dominated Mercyhurst, 52-0, to open dual competition at Cameron High School in Cameron, W.Va., on Saturday.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/7/Wrestling_vsMercyhurst_atCameron_Nov7_2026_AM-50.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:56:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>18</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59706</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Come Up Short in Five-Set Battle with UCF</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/volleyball-mountaineers-come-up-short-in-five-set-battle-with-ucf</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/volleyball-mountaineers-come-up-short-in-five-set-battle-with-ucf</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia volleyball loses to UCF in five sets in Morgantown" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/15/DAK08670.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (13-11, 6-8 Big 12) fell to UCF, 3-2, on Sunday afternoon inside Hope Coliseum. The Mountaineers dropped the five-set match by scores of 25-18, 22-25, 26-28, 25-20 and 11-15.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/15/DAK08670.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/15/DAK08670.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia volleyball loses to UCF in five sets in Morgantown</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/15/DAK08670.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:10:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59705</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Finish First at WVU Fall Classic</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/rifle-mountaineers-finish-first-at-wvu-fall-classic</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/rifle-mountaineers-finish-first-at-wvu-fall-classic</guid><category>Rifle</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Jennifer Kocher on the line during the WVU Fall Classic" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/15/WVU08491.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 1-ranked West Virginia University rifle team finished in first place at the WVU Fall Classic with a team score of 4757 on Sunday afternoon, at the Bill McKenzie Rifle Range inside the WVU Shell Building in Morgantown.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/15/WVU08491.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/15/WVU08491.jpg"><media:title>Jennifer Kocher on the line during the WVU Fall Classic</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/15/WVU08491.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:19:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>8</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59704</s:story_id></item><item><title>Houston Game to be Televised on TNT/TruTV/HBO MAX at 1 p.m., ET</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/football-houston-game-to-be-televised-on-tnt-trutv-hbo-max-at-1-pm-et</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/15/football-houston-game-to-be-televised-on-tnt-trutv-hbo-max-at-1-pm-et</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The blue West Virginia football helmet on the field at Mountaineer Field at Milan Puskar Stadium before West Virginia's game against Cincinnati on Oct. 17, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/17/10-17-26-HELMET-2.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The Big 12 Conference has announced that WVU's Nov. 21 football game against No. 14/16 Houston at Milan Puskar Stadium will be televised on TNT and will be simulcast on TruTV and HBO MAX at 1 p.m., ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/10-17-26-HELMET-2.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/10-17-26-HELMET-2.jpg"><media:title>The blue West Virginia football helmet on the field at Mountaineer Field at Milan Puskar Stadium before West Virginia's game against Cincinnati on Oct. 17, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/10-17-26-HELMET-2.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:12:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59703</s:story_id></item><item><title>West Virginia Falls to Kansas on Saturday at Milan Puskar Stadium</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/14/football-west-virginia-falls-to-kansas-on-saturday-at-milan-puskar-stadium</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/14/football-west-virginia-falls-to-kansas-on-saturday-at-milan-puskar-stadium</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia quarterback Michael Hawkins Jr. scores his 20th rushing touchdown of the season in West Virginia's game against Kansas at Milan Puskar Stadium on Saturday, Nov. 14, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/14/Hawkins-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Kansas used dominant offensive and defensive efforts to dispose of West Virginia 37-14 on Saturday at Milan Puskar Stadium.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/14/Hawkins-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/14/Hawkins-Main.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia quarterbac